$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM C. Procedure for three-step sequence (Scheme 1) To a sample vial (4 mL)
equipped with a Teflon-coated stirbar were added in sequence iron powder
(25 µmol), NBS (0.75 mmol), 4-chloroanisole (0.50 mmol) and deionized
water (1 mL). The vial was covered with a phenolic cap and the contents
stirred on a reaction block preheated to 50 °C, and the reaction
monitored by GCMS. After complete consumption of the starting material,
the contents were brought to rt and to the same vial were added
PdCl2(dtbpf) (10 µmol), aryl boronic acid (0.60 mmol) and Et3N (1.50
mmol). The contents were stirred at 50 °C for 3 h with monitoring by
GCMS. After completion of the cross-coupling, the contents were brought
to rt and to the same vial was added TMDS (1.0 mmol). The contents were
stirred again at 50 °C until complete dehalogenation. The contents were
brought to rt and extracted with EtOAc. The organic extract was
concentrated in vacuo and purified by flash chromatography over silica
gel with EtOAc/hexanes to obtain pure product.
2,3-Difluoro-2'-methoxy-1,1'-biphenyl (Scheme 1, compound 8) Yield: 90.2
mg, 82% (for the final dehalogenation it was left for 12 h); yellowish
solid; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.42-7.37 (m, 1H), 7.28 - 7.23 (m, 1H),
7.20 - 7.06 (m, 3H), 7.07 - 6.96 (m, 2H), 3.82 (s, 3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, safety (dihydrogen generated),
bromination/Suzuki-Miyauracoupling/dechlorination sequence, in-situ
generated reagent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Ligand-Free, Palladium-Catalyzed Dihydrogen Generation from TMDS:
Dehalogenation of Aryl Halides on Water
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Bhattacharjya, Anish; Klumphu, Piyatida; Lipshutz, Bruce H.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2015), 17(5), 1122-1125

